.TH HYPRMONCFGD 1 "@MAN_DATE@" "hyprmoncfg @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprmoncfgd \- automatically apply Hyprland monitor profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprmoncfgd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprmoncfgd
monitors display topology and laptop lid changes, selects the best matching
profile saved by
.BR hyprmoncfg (1),
and applies it through the same verified apply engine used by the interactive
program.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config-dir " directory
Use an alternative profile configuration directory.
.TP
.BI "--debounce " duration
Wait this long before applying a profile after a change. The default is 1.2s.
.TP
.BI "--poll-interval " duration
Poll for monitor changes at this interval. The default is 5s.
.TP
.BI "--lid-poll-interval " duration
Poll the laptop lid state at this interval when event detection is unavailable.
The default is 1s.
.TP
.BI "--wake-settle " duration
Wait for display topology to settle after wake before applying a profile. The
default is 2s.
.TP
.BI "--profile " name
Always apply the named profile instead of automatically matching one.
.TP
.BI "--monitors-conf " file
Write the generated monitor configuration to an alternative path.
.TP
.BI "--hypr-config " file
Use an alternative Hyprland root configuration for include verification.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress daemon log messages.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show the program version.
.SH SERVICE
The package installs a systemd user service. Enable it explicitly with:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user enable --now hyprmoncfgd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprmoncfg (1),
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Full documentation is available at https://hyprmoncfg.dev.
